ts overall mass.\nTherefore, the part of an atom that has the least mass is the electron.\nThe best answer is A.<|eot_id|>", "new_cot_probs": [1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "cot_prob": [-0.6035081148147583], "cot_step_prob": [-0.7168571949005127]}, "4": {"completion": "A): electron. Electrons have the least mass", "probs": [0.457785964012146, 0.457785964012146, 0.05467473715543747, 0.022791819646954536], "prediction": 0, "target_cot_step": "To answer this, we need to consider the masses of the different parts of an atom.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: Which part of an atom has the least mass?\n\nChoices:\n(A): electron\n(B): nucleus\n(C): neutron\n(D): proton\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\nThe question asks for the part of an atom with the least mass.", "specificity_preds": [1, 2, 0, 1, 3, 2, 1, 2, 2, 0, 0, 2, 2, 1, 3, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1], "specificity_probs": [[0.015596557408571243, 0.9649248719215393, 0.015596557408571243, 0.0004709752683993429], [0.46060997247695923, 0.012274839915335178, 0.5219394564628601, 0.0012937586288899183], [0.974917471408844, 0.010830354876816273, 0.001882033422589302, 0.002416578819975257], [0.17172129452228546, 0.7696014642715454, 0.04341794550418854, 0.01243944838643074], [0.19216303527355194, 0.037839144468307495, 0.004519241396337748, 0.7600195407867432], [0.15792199969291687, 0.09578453004360199, 0.7077572345733643, 0.035237159579992294], [0.07570453733205795, 0.6338663101196289, 0.16026648879051208, 0.12481566518545151], [0.0010884295916184783, 0.0006201685173436999, 0.9895358681678772, 0.001158627332188189], [0.0008940708357840776, 0.012342266738414764, 0.980467677116394, 0.0006963030318729579], [0.7414278984069824, 0.08855094015598297, 0.022389182820916176, 0.14599579572677612], [0.9593076109886169, 0.019909793511033058, 0.006463763769716024, 0.007324403617531061], [0.1851126104593277, 0.2693372666835785, 0.30519911646842957, 0.2376893013715744], [0.002452470362186432, 0.0008475509821437299, 0.9893970489501953, 0.00